2026-10-28T17:15:42.2809752Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019UJiiLuU8LnoPnExw34fi9","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 10,\n    \"title\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan: Create fails/hangs and never persists to state for No Upfront plans and future purchase_time\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": [\n      \"bug\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-08-03T16:26:27+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": \"Report a Bug\",\n    \"missing_required\": [],\n    \"empty_optional\": [],\n    \"used_form\": true\n  },\n  \"services\": {\n    \"resources_mentioned\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": true,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/savingsplans\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_savingsplans_offerings\",\n        \"resource_exists\": false,\n        \"data_source_exists\": true,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/savingsplans\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"regex_labeler_would_apply\": [\n      \"bug\",\n      \"service/savingsplans\"\n    ],\n    \"primary_service_label\": \"service/savingsplans\"\n  },\n  \"versions\": {\n    \"terraform\": \"1.15.8\",\n    \"provider\": \"6.57.1\",\n    \"latest_release\": \"6.57.1\",\n    \"latest_release_date\": \"2026-07-29\",\n    \"provider_status\": \"current\",\n    \"minor_releases_behind\": 0,\n    \"newer_release_notes\": [],\n    \"newer_fixes\": []\n  },\n  \"similar_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 47519,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#47519\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan: Create times out when purchase_time is set to a future date (Queued state not treated as completion)\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_savingsplans_savings_plan When purchase_time is set to a future date, the Savings Plan is placed in queued state by the AWS API. This is the correct and final state until the scheduled purchase date arrives. The terraform apply should complete successfully, treating queued as a valid terminal state for scheduled purchases. terraform apply hangs during creation and eventually fails with a tim\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-04-18T17:40:01Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.435,\n      \"band\": \"likely\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 48394,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#48394\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan fails after creating No Upfront plan because upfront_payment_amount changes from null to \\\"0.00000000\\\"\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan If the user creates a no-upfront savings plan, it should successfully apply and produce a consistent result. Creating a no-upfront savings plan produces an output of \\\"upfront_payment_amount = 0.00000000\\\" after create, which causes Terraform to treat the resource as tainted. console Provider produced inconsistent result after apply .upfront_payment_amount: was null, bu\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-06-12T20:06:03Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.387,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46381,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46381\",\n      \"title\": \"Importing `aws_savingsplans_savingsplan` resource is missing `savings_plan_offering_id` and `purchase_time`\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_savingsplans_savings_plan There should be no force-replacement with same savings_plan_offering_id and purchase_time of the Savings Plan. After importing the Savings plan, terraform always marked the resource for the force-replacement. console Click to expand configuration hcl # module.compute_savings_plan[\\\"compute-2025-07-21-3y-all-upfront\\\"].aws_savingsplans_savings_plan.this must be replace\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T13:39:15Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.318,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 46382,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#46382\",\n      \"title\": \"Importing `aws_savingsplans_savingsplan` resource triggers forced-replacement by `upfront_payment_amount` property\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_savingsplans_savings_plan upfront_payment_amount property cannot be configured by user. So this property shouldn't trigger forced-replacement It triggers forced-replacement console Click to expand configuration hcl # module.compute_savings_plan[\\\"compute-2025-07-21-3y-all-upfront\\\"].aws_savingsplans_savings_plan.this must be replaced -/+ resource \\\"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan\\\" \\\"this\\\" { ~ curr\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-09T13:42:31Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.272,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 48393,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#48393\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan produces inconsistent result when AWS normalizes commitment decimal places\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"aws_savingsplans_savings_plan The provider should normalize the configured commitment value, or otherwise treat \\\"1.158\\\" and \\\"1.15800000\\\" as equivalent. AWS creates the Savings Plan, but Terraform fails the apply because the provider returns a different string value than the planned value. console Provider produced inconsistent result after apply .commitment: was cty.StringVal(\\\"1.158\\\"), but now cty\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-06-12T20:02:40Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.188,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11478,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04470344-e8a7-